# An orthographic camera (ABI 1.20, strata_camera_ortho) looking down at 45
# degrees from the south-east, as an isometric game or a map view does, over
# a 7 x 7 grid of pillars in the afternoon sun with four cascades. The
# cascades are fitted to the box the camera sees rather than to a perspective
# frustum, so every pillar, near the bottom of the frame or far at the top,
# casts a crisp shadow; the far rows sit in later cascades. The sky has no
# perspective to show and is one colour. Pillars do not shrink with distance.
size 480 270
camera_ortho 30 30 30  0 0 0  13 1 200
lighting sun 0.62 35  4 2048 120 0.6 1
clear 0 0 0 1 sky
item cube 0 -0.5 0  60 1 60  0.55 0.62 0.45
item cube -12 2 -12  1.4 4 1.4  0.82 0.78 0.70
item cube -12 3 -8  1.4 6 1.4  0.82 0.78 0.70
item cube -12 1 -4  1.4 2 1.4  0.82 0.78 0.70
item cube -12 2 0  1.4 4 1.4  0.82 0.78 0.70
